  "solution": "Given:\n\n x⁴+(1)/(x⁴)=47\n\nConcept used:\n\n1. (a + b)² - 2ab = a² + b²\n\n2. (a + b)³ = a³ + b³ + 3ab(a + b)\n\nCalculation:\n\nAccording to the concept,\n\n x⁴+(1)/(x⁴)=47\n\n⇒ (x²+(1)/(x²))² - 2 × x² × (1)/(x²)=47\n\n⇒ (x²+(1)/(x²))² - 2 =47\n\n⇒ (x²+(1)/(x²))² = 47 + 2\n\n⇒ (x²+(1)/(x²))² = 49\n\n⇒ (x²+(1)/(x²)) = 7\n\n⇒ (x +(1)/(x))² - 2 × x × (1)/(x) = 7\n\n⇒ (x +(1)/(x))² - 2 = 7\n\n⇒ (x +(1)/(x))² = 7 + 2\n\n⇒ (x +(1)/(x))² = 9\n\n⇒ (x +(1)/(x)) = 3 ....(1)\n\n⇒ (x +(1)/(x))³ = 3³\n\n⇒ x³ +(1)/(x³) + 3x × frac {1}{x} (x + frac {1}{x}) = 3³\n\n⇒ x³ +(1)/(x³) + 3 × 3 = 3³ (From 1)\n\n⇒ x³ +(1)/(x³) = 27 - 9\n\n⇒ x³ +(1)/(x³) = 18\n\n**∴ The value of x³+(1)/(x³) is 18.**\n\n [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/ca81259519cadfb2d5350673c220e419e60378e9770ad26512fc8e826a8d93f1.png] **__Shortcut Trick__**Ifx4 + 1/x4 = P, then x² + 1/x² = √(P + 2) = Q\n\nAnd x + 1/x = √(Q + 2) = S\n\nx³ + 1/x³ = S³ - 3S \n\nNow, x⁴ + 1/x⁴ = 47\n\nx2 + 1/x2 = √(47 + 2) = √49 = 7\n\nx + 1/x = √(7 + 2) = √9 = 3\n\nx3 + 1/x3 = 33 - 3 × 3 \n\n⇒ 27 - 9 = 18\n\n**∴ x3 + 1/x3 is 18.**\n\n133:",
